  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246086",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "sourceHash": "b03ef12fe850d417c03421f3b615a5c6786e5b620808847c550bc1eced19a5ad",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.251,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "Maximilian And that's now it for form actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "These are the core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 10.8,
          "en": "form actions related features React offers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.8,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "And the key takeaway they offer is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "that you can define functions which you can pass as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 21.003,
          "en": "for the action prompt to form elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.23,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "or as you learned to buttons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "and then there the formAction prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "and React will then make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "that these action functions are invoked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "and it will give you the form data automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "So it will automatically collect all the input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "and give you such a form data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 45.18,
          "en": "It will also automatically reset the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 46.86,
          "en": "which can be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.86,
          "end": 50.44,
          "en": "And that's why you also might want to use useActionState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.833,
          "en": "so that your form action can return a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.67,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "any value of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 60.87,
          "en": "Can be a object, as is the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 62.253,
          "en": "but doesn't have to be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "And then you can use that form state to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "to show some error messages, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "but also to pre-populate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "or repopulate those input fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 80.613,
          "en": "with the values entered by the user, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "And you can do anything you want in your form actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 88.53,
          "en": "You can store the code in local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.53,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "if you want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "But you can also, of course, use context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 94.22999999999999,
          "en": "or directly send a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "from inside the form action if you want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 99.15299999999999,
          "en": "to send the data to a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "because form actions can be async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 107.22,
          "en": "They don't have to be, as you also saw in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.22,
          "end": 108.453,
          "en": "but they can be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "And if they are async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 114.03,
          "en": "and if they potentially take a bit longer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.03,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "you got additional hooks like you useFormStatus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "which you can use to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 121.863,
          "en": "whilst the form is being submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123,
          "end": 127.23,
          "en": "And you got useOptimistic to perform Optimistic updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.23,
          "end": 131.55,
          "en": "So to set some temporary state, some temporary value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.55,
          "end": 133.89,
          "en": "which will automatically be thrown away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.89,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "once the form submission is over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 138.873,
          "en": "so once the action function is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.8,
          "end": 142.77,
          "en": "You can use all these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.77,
          "end": 146.793,
          "en": "thanks to this form actions feature that's built into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.84,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "Now when it comes to handling form submissions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "it's therefore, of course, is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "whether you want to use form actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "or whether you want to handle submissions manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 161.16,
          "en": "with help of the on submit prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.16,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "and by preventing the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "and by using all these things you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 168.48,
          "en": "in the previous course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 171.39,
          "en": "because that's also absolutely valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 173.79,
          "en": "You don't have to use form actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 175.59300000000002,
          "en": "but of course, you can.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}